Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?P39:=20pgm=5Fbase=20=E2=80=94=20register=20only?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20PNG/JPEG/BMP=20image=20handlers=20in=20headless?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

wxInitAllImageHandlers() registers 11+ wxImageHandler subclasses:
PNG, JPEG, BMP, GIF, TIFF, TGA, XPM, PCX, PNM, IFF, ANI, ICO, PICT,
XBM. Each is a static ctor + wxImage::AddHandler call + a factory
registration.

For kicad-cli, only PNG/JPEG/BMP are relevant:
- PNG: pcb render output + embedded board images
- JPEG: pcb render output + embedded board images
- BMP: bitmap2component reads and writes bitmaps

Register just those three in headless; keep wxInitAllImageHandlers
for GUI. Small per-startup save, plus a smaller RSS footprint from
not loading the codec libs the extra handlers might dlopen lazily.
---
 common/pgm_base.cpp | 22 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/common/pgm_base.cpp b/common/pgm_base.cpp
index fc14ed0b..aeaf992a 100644
--- a/common/pgm_base.cpp
+++ b/common/pgm_base.cpp
@@ -28,6 +28,9 @@
 
 #include <wx/html/htmlwin.h>
 #include <wx/fs_zip.h>
+#include <wx/imagbmp.h>
+#include <wx/imagjpeg.h>
+#include <wx/imagpng.h>
 #include <wx/dir.h>
 #include <wx/filename.h>
 #include <wx/msgdlg.h>
@@ -378,7 +381,24 @@ bool PGM_BASE::InitPgm( bool aHeadless, bool aIsUnitTest )
     if( !aHeadless )
         APP_MONITOR::SENTRY::Instance()->AddTag( "kicad.app", pgm_name );
 
-    wxInitAllImageHandlers();
+    // Perf: GUI needs all wx image handlers (menu icons, drag-drop of
+    // any image type, wxPropertyGrid displaying anything). Headless
+    // kicad-cli only ever reads PNG/JPEG (embedded board images, PCB
+    // render output) and only ever writes PNG/JPEG — the other handlers
+    // (GIF, TIFF, TGA, XPM, PCX, PNM, IFF, ANI, ICO, PICT, XBM) each
+    // register themselves via a static ctor + wxImage::AddHandler call.
+    // Register only the minimal set in headless mode; behaviour for the
+    // supported plot/render formats is unchanged.
+    if( aHeadless )
+    {
+        wxImage::AddHandler( new wxPNGHandler );
+        wxImage::AddHandler( new wxJPEGHandler );
+        wxImage::AddHandler( new wxBMPHandler );
+    }
+    else
+    {
+        wxInitAllImageHandlers();
+    }
 
 #if !wxCHECK_VERSION( 3, 3, 0 )
     // Without this the wxPropertyGridManager segfaults on Windows.
